      ['A hummingbird with a rose-pink throat and crown that has spread north thanks to garden flowers and feeders, now wintering as far as Canada. Males dive from up to 40 m in courtship, pulling out of the dive at over 20 body lengths a second, one of the fastest movements relative to size of any animal; their tail feathers make a loud chirp.'],
