      ['A camouflaged, owl-like bird that spends the day motionless on the ground or along a branch, looking like bark. At dusk the male makes a long, mechanical churring song and flies after moths with its huge, bristle-fringed mouth. Its old name “goatsucker” comes from the false belief that it drank milk from goats.'],
